@startuml MaintenanceRecordSequence
!include style.puml
hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 170

title eqm-maintain e/001 date/27-10-26 work/Repair outcome/Completed

participant ":Parser" as Parser
participant ":EqmManager" as Manager
participant ":MaintenanceHandler" as Handler
participant ":EquipmentHandler" as Inventory
participant "item:Equipment" as Item
participant "record:MaintenanceRecord" as Record
participant "MaintenanceStorage" as Storage <<utility>>

note over Parser, Manager
One iteration of run(); startup succeeded.
Maintenance storage is configured.
end note
Manager -> Parser : getInput()
[-> Parser : user input
Parser --> Manager : input
Manager -> Manager : executeInput(input)
Manager -> Manager : recordMaintenance(...)
Manager -> Handler : addMaintenanceRecord(input)
activate Handler

alt validation fails (details summarised)
    note over Handler, Item
    Stop at the first rejection: parseCommand(input),
    isFutureDate(parsed.date()), missing equipment,
    or MaintenanceRecord constructor validation.
    No save; existing records and file unchanged.
    end note
    Handler --> Manager : throws MaintenanceRecordUnsuccessful
    Manager -> Manager : ConsoleOutput.error(message)
else validation succeeds
    Handler -> Handler : parseCommand(input)
    Handler -> Handler : isFutureDate(\nparsed.date())
    Handler -> Inventory : getEquipmentById(\nparsed.itemId())
    Inventory --> Handler : item
    Handler -> Item : getRecordId()
    Item --> Handler : permanent UUID string
    create Record
    Handler -> Record : new MaintenanceRecord(...)
    note over Record
    UUID from item.getRecordId();
    date, work, outcome from parsed.
    Constructor validates values.
    end note
    Handler -> Handler : copy records; add record to proposedRecords
    Handler -> Handler : save(proposedRecords)
    Handler -> Storage : save(storageFile, proposedRecords)
    activate Storage
    note over Storage
    Files.createDirectories(parent)
    Files.createTempFile(...)
    toStorageLine(record) for each entry
    Files.write(..., UTF_8)
    Files.move(..., REPLACE_EXISTING)
    Finally: Files.deleteIfExists(...).
    end note
    alt save returns normally
        Storage --> Handler : saved
        Handler -> Handler : records.add(record)
        Handler --> Manager : record
        Manager -> Manager : ConsoleOutput.success(...)
        Manager -> Manager : display item, date, work and outcome
    else IOException during save
        Storage --> Handler : throws IOException
        note over Handler, Storage
        Live records unchanged; log WARNING.
        A failure before replacement preserves the old file.
        Replacement is not atomic; no file rollback is implemented.
        end note
        Handler --> Manager : throws MaintenanceRecordUnsuccessful
        Manager -> Manager : ConsoleOutput.error(message)
    end
    deactivate Storage
end
deactivate Handler
@enduml
